  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: Annihilator theory of Kⁿ as a K[X]-module via M. Module annihilator = span{minpoly K M}; vecAnnIdeal M v = span{minpoly K M} for a cyclic vector (deg minpoly = n), via monic polynomial division f = q·minpoly + r with the cyclic property killing r; monicity from Cayley-Hamilton integrality. 6 theorems, 2 defs, 145 lines, 0 sorries, 0 axioms. Repaired bit-rot (LinearMap.mul_apply → Module.End.mul_apply) and added gallery data for an orphaned proof.",
    "builtItems": [
      "kn_module_annihilator_eq_minpoly: K[X]-annihilator of Kⁿ = span{minpoly K M}",
      "vecAnnIdeal: annihilator ideal {f : f(M)·v = 0} of a vector",
      "mem_vecAnnIdeal_iff: membership via the AEval' scalar action",
      "minpoly_mem_vecAnnIdeal / minpoly_ideal_le_vecAnnIdeal: span{minpoly K M} ≤ vecAnnIdeal M v",
      "IsCyclicVector + cyclic_vecAnnIdeal_eq_minpoly: cyclic v ⟹ vecAnnIdeal M v = span{minpoly K M}"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Fixing M makes Kⁿ a K[X]-module; annihilators become ideals of the PID K[X].",
      "A vector's order divides the minimal polynomial and equals it exactly for cyclic vectors.",
      "Cyclicity makes the remainder of monic division vanish, upgrading span{minpoly} ≤ vecAnnIdeal to equality.",
      "Monicity of the minimal polynomial follows for free from Cayley-Hamilton (integrality of M)."
